            "queryable": true,
            "ontology": null,
            "documentation": "A value cell for a fraction: a part of a whole, such as the share of a test's time spent in an arm (Jess Haley 2026-10-26 [fraction value kind]; T12). Canonical as a plain ratio (1 = the whole; om:one), plus the lossless source: a percent is kept as written in `source_value` with `source_unit` om:percent. Not a `score`: a score is a rating on a named rubric, a fraction is a ratio that means the same in every dataset. Series-as-cardinality: an array of the cell; per-sample timing is a time covariate along a time dimension (`dimensions` / `covariates`: the statement's when inline, each body's otherwise).",
            "constraints": {},
            "fields": [
                {
                    "name": "fraction",
                    "type": "double",
                    "blank_value": 0.0,
                    "default_value": 0.0,
                    "mustBeNonEmpty": false,
                    "mustBeScalar": true,
                    "mustNotHaveNaN": false,
                    "queryable": true,
                    "ontology": null,
                    "documentation": "Canonical fraction, as a plain ratio: 1 is the whole, 0.25 a quarter (om:one). Not bounded above: a part may exceed its reference whole. Absent only when the run's migration report lists it as a gap ([gap accepted when the report lists it]; the source gave no unit, or a unit with no conversion; `source_value` and `source_unit` keep what the source wrote) -- Jess Haley 2026-10-30 [canonical absent only as needs info].",
